#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198392 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198034 :question/id #uuid "b81eb0cb-a740-5e86-921c-4baa8c179e55" :question/math-academy-id "e-12387" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $y = h(x,z)$ for $(x,z) \\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) = \\left\\langle P,\\: Q,\\: R \\right\\rangle$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \n\\Bigg( \n\\bbox[3pt, border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}} \\dfrac{\\partial h}{\\partial x} \n+ Q \n- \\bbox[3pt, border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}} \\dfrac{\\partial h}{\\partial z}\n\\Bigg) \\: \\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?\n\n*Hint: The orientation of $S$ should be chosen such that the unit normal vector has a positive  $\\mathbf j$-component.*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $y = h(x,z),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(x,z) = \\left\\langle x, \\: h(x,z),\\: z \\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨0,\\frac{∂h}{∂z},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & \\frac{∂h}{∂x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{∂h}{∂z} & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,-1,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂z}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, notice that the $\\mathbf j$-component is negative. Therefore, we select the normal vector that points in the *opposite* direction:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}'_z \\times \\mathbf{r}'_x = - \\mathbf{r}'_x \\times \\mathbf{r}'_z =   \\left \\langle -\\dfrac{\\partial h}{\\partial x}, \\: 1, \\: -\\dfrac{\\partial h}{\\partial z} \\right \\rangle\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,z))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,1,\\,-\\frac{∂h}{∂z}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂h}{∂x}+Q-R\\frac{∂h}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "55cd2fdb-4cae-5f0b-bea0-e845d51190e1" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049883 :topic/math-academy-id 1264 :topic/title "Surface Integrals Over Cartesian Surfaces"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198602 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ae2d92e-ed1f-5f54-9f3e-4ce38b8da70d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-P,\\,$ $∂P,\\,$ $∂x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275570} {:answer/id #uuid "2786ad1c-2c77-5044-8bba-022ff896dea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P,\\,$ $∂g,\\,$ $∂x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275839} {:answer/id #uuid "44ac2a5e-f444-5ab8-8d2f-b1befe6ae68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-P,\\,$ $∂g,\\,$ $∂x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276081} {:answer/id #uuid "4e5bb47b-fd98-5623-8225-b6a60c57026d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P,\\,$ $∂g,\\,$ $∂y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276170} {:answer/id #uuid "8b5ef7c7-aca0-5aa4-b9ce-95d7314ff4ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-P,\\,$ $∂g,\\,$ $∂y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b5ef7c7-aca0-5aa4-b9ce-95d7314ff4ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-P,\\,$ $∂g,\\,$ $∂y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276743} :answer-field/id #uuid "62e5c477-cfc8-5f60-94c2-948eec13a409" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277901}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9923f940-6e67-51d8-8336-d46f1ce02fd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161166" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\frac{}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z=g(x,y),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,g(x,y)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198605 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05adf01e-c7b1-5e97-b5eb-3f2025764ada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275527} {:answer/id #uuid "54638f1d-1303-5a95-ba48-da06bfbcee4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-P$ and $Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276226} {:answer/id #uuid "57c6c235-25f5-5f19-a313-895f424e6c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $P$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276263} {:answer/id #uuid "74d9839f-a860-523e-923f-a6741e1f1d1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $-Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276535} {:answer/id #uuid "f604d50d-71c4-5c4d-a5df-37fe3a24fd07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-P$ and $-Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f604d50d-71c4-5c4d-a5df-37fe3a24fd07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-P$ and $-Q$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277629} :answer-field/id #uuid "1de77bc5-7a01-5bd2-8ed1-6d5e7458e367" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277779}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b8aa780b-8e8f-52b7-b96a-66254bcb10c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161189" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂g}{∂x}+\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z=g(x,y),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,g(x,y)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}+(-Q\\,)\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278512 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7082e8bb-b180-5b74-b8a7-e85890274ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-Q$ and $∂z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276491} {:answer/id #uuid "90563b64-bf19-5230-a35a-721a99920cf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-Q$ and $∂x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276784} {:answer/id #uuid "91780ef2-9a71-57a1-99ea-245bc6f522d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $∂x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276795} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8f03ec-bd00-5c8c-b9b2-ca5f6b5f96f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $∂z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277155} {:answer/id #uuid "ed73198a-0a2c-58e6-bfa9-608aaaadffc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-R$ and $∂z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7082e8bb-b180-5b74-b8a7-e85890274ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-Q$ and $∂z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276491} :answer-field/id #uuid "2729d011-05e6-5f9a-aa2c-45fe935285a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277789}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1aa60ad7-eedc-5a6c-9adc-f826e8cc15e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161446" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $x=k(y,z)$ for $(y,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(P+\\frac{∂k}{∂y}-R\\frac{∂k}{})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $x=k(y,z),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(y,z)=⟨k(y,z),\\,y,\\,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂k}{∂z},\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂k}{∂y} & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{∂k}{∂z} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨1,\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂z}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂z}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(P+(-Q\\,)\\frac{∂k}{∂y}-R\\frac{∂k}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278515 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0643aa87-cd34-546b-808f-baf7069ddd3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2P$ and $R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275535} {:answer/id #uuid "33a51edf-b815-559f-bf1a-c079952737b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $-2R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275936} {:answer/id #uuid "363514bb-3d3f-5b6d-8842-2ca7a25acfe7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275960} {:answer/id #uuid "608d35ab-75b6-598e-b2f0-82ca279404a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2P$ and $2R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276340} {:answer/id #uuid "fb6360fb-9cce-5dca-8b8d-0788f42c0291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2P$ and $-2R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0643aa87-cd34-546b-808f-baf7069ddd3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2P$ and $R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275535} :answer-field/id #uuid "3292da62-41fc-5075-93e6-a9828fa8aabd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277805}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ce5730b3-fc65-5b4c-bdd5-95a34bf939c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161453" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $y=-{x}^{2}z$ for $(x,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\,xz+Q+\\,{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?\n\n*Hint: The orientation of $S$ should be chosen such that the unit normal vector has a positive  $j$-component.*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $y=-{x}^{2}z,$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,z)=⟨x,\\,-{x}^{2}z,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,-2xz,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,-{x}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2xz & 0 \\\\ 0 & -{x}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨-2xz,\\,-1,\\,-{x}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, notice that the $j$-component is negative. Therefore, we select the normal vector that points in the *opposite* direction:\n\n$$\n{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{x}^{′}=-{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′}=⟨2xz,\\,1,\\,{x}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,z))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,R\\,⟩\\cdot ⟨2xz,\\,1,\\,{x}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2P\\,xz+Q+R\\,{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278516 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1030e7c9-e96e-503f-967b-785d007daa76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2Q$ and $R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275620} {:answer/id #uuid "144499aa-4e39-58cc-9e9a-8a50dd3383d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2Q$ and $-2R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275665} {:answer/id #uuid "68ab0b1a-abea-51fe-b67c-1548bc01d191" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276417} {:answer/id #uuid "a76e424f-dd86-5864-94a5-584b2a311108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $-2R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276987} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b4e30b-9426-50d8-bc2f-4878ecf2feae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-Q$ and $-R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "144499aa-4e39-58cc-9e9a-8a50dd3383d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2Q$ and $-2R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275665} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e4956ee-4770-5be1-83ec-b19c8e91c7c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277890}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a6603224-9e78-54fd-8272-af20dda792ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-161456" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $x=2yz$ for $(y,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(P+\\,z+\\,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $x=2yz,$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(y,z)=⟨2yz,\\,y,\\,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨2z,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨2y,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2z & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2y & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨1,\\,-2z,\\,-2y⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(y,z))\\cdot ({r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-2z,\\,-2y⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(P+(\\,-2Q)\\,z+(\\,-2R)\\,y\\,)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278519 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11e71243-92a0-5d43-b5a3-d37e9d9577d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275638} {:answer/id #uuid "1733f81c-8c75-5995-ad54-2ab255bb13b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂x},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275694} {:answer/id #uuid "2cfc931d-121f-57c0-ac5c-fdc2916d3343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275883} {:answer/id #uuid "3a8033d3-73a6-5faf-9ba8-27ae7a3acd02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275991} {:answer/id #uuid "4f2411ed-300b-54b9-9625-f35ce1fd17dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f2411ed-300b-54b9-9625-f35ce1fd17dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q,\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\text{ }\\frac{∂k}{∂z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276182} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fceae9a-bc1a-5dd0-a3ba-10a17494da0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277822}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "46dbd1e0-5399-5e33-b950-1f08b8d717ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-161465" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $x=k(y,z)$ for $(y,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(P-\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}-R\\,\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $x=k(y,z),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(y,z)=⟨k(y,z),\\,y,\\,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂k}{∂z},\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂k}{∂y} & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{∂k}{∂z} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨1,\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂z}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂y},\\,-\\frac{∂k}{∂z}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(P-Q\\,\\frac{∂k}{∂y}-R\\,\\frac{∂k}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373979 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "333cd0c0-ea57-5e53-975d-79f76fb18013" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "P,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂z},\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373981} {:answer/id #uuid "9ac4e1a7-5360-5598-85dd-70d2cbb3cd86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-P,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373982} {:answer/id #uuid "1e3427ae-61e2-5bd9-9b34-c9a3c4f9f4ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-P,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂y},\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373983} {:answer/id #uuid "d4c19d76-6f69-56ba-b90f-4e4dfe1d7922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-P,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373984} {:answer/id #uuid "24bbe4da-5bb4-5f04-bd1a-ef46ed95ade9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-P,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂y},\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4c19d76-6f69-56ba-b90f-4e4dfe1d7922" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-P,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373984} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c9eea5b-e0c0-5c9a-bb50-8a16e942de63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373980}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "54d448ec-919c-5c61-a65c-48a634770024" :question/math-academy-id "q-161460" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $y=h(x,z)$ for $(x,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\,+Q-R\\,)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?\n\n*Hint: The orientation of $S$ should be chosen such that the unit normal vector has a positive  $j$-component.*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $y=h(x,z),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,z)=⟨x,\\,h(x,z),\\,z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨0,\\frac{∂h}{∂z},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & \\frac{∂h}{∂x} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{∂h}{∂z} & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,-1,\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂z}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, notice that the $j$-component is negative. Therefore, we select the normal vector that points in the *opposite* direction:\n\n$$\n{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{x}^{′}=-{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′}=⟨-\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,1,\\,-\\frac{∂h}{∂z}⟩\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,z))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂h}{∂x},\\,1,\\,-\\frac{∂h}{∂z}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂x}+Q-R\\,\\frac{∂h}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401240 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b6ce404-ebcc-51cc-943b-4e4e79eb614d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2R$ and $-2P$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401242} {:answer/id #uuid "44cf614b-483e-57c6-b48c-bdea43bdf8c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401243} {:answer/id #uuid "920e8870-c9e3-5c16-bd67-bc6987066749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $-6R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401244} {:answer/id #uuid "7051dd66-a8a1-5bd2-a47a-cbbfa2e9ad6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2P$ and $-R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401245} {:answer/id #uuid "23d98ea3-b274-5a12-a721-30dfede024ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2P$ and $6R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23d98ea3-b274-5a12-a721-30dfede024ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-2P$ and $6R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401246} :answer-field/id #uuid "d028cbae-7e56-54b5-84a6-c407d88b99d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401241}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "75438633-2fed-5dc6-8f93-bd3571d872a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161455" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $y=2x{z}^{3}$ for $(x,z)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,{z}^{3}+Q-\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,x{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?\n\n*Hint: The orientation of $S$ should be chosen such that the unit normal vector has a positive  $j$-component.*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $y=2x{z}^{3},$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,z)=⟨x,\\,2x{z}^{3},z⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,2{z}^{3},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,6x{z}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2{z}^{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6x{z}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|=⟨2{z}^{3},\\,-1,\\,6x{z}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, notice that the $j$-component is negative. Therefore, we select the normal vector that points in the *opposite* direction:\n\n$$\n{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{x}^{′}=-{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{z}^{′}=⟨-2{z}^{3},\\,1,\\,-6x{z}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,z))\\cdot ({r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{x}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,R\\,⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{z}^{3},\\,1,\\,-6x{z}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2P\\,{z}^{3}+Q-6R\\,x{z}^{2}\\,)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401247 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4fc5fe-cb91-578b-8dbf-4a5ffd8c3fd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∂g,\\text{ }-Q,\\text{ }∂Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401249} {:answer/id #uuid "1b9077fe-1593-50c2-8f89-3d6b0dcabdfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∂g,\\text{ }Q,\\text{ }∂z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401250} {:answer/id #uuid "1c8485ee-e4b0-5c7e-96b8-4bdcc10e86bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∂g,\\text{ }-Q,\\text{ }∂z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401251} {:answer/id #uuid "09583e22-9aba-582a-80e6-e8808ccbeebf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∂g,\\text{ }-Q,\\text{ }∂y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401252} {:answer/id #uuid "3581b172-6284-5dbd-9767-909757324a62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∂g,\\text{ }Q,\\text{ }∂y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3581b172-6284-5dbd-9767-909757324a62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "∂g,\\text{ }Q,\\text{ }∂y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401253} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ee6b27a-bcd5-52e8-9493-e839011ba707" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401248}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "417f7e3b-659c-5f7d-913c-decf384148f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161457" :question/problem "For a surface $S$ given by $z=g(x,y)$ for $(x,y)\\in D,$ the flux of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}{∂x}-\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\frac{∂g}{\\bbox[3pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the formula?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nSince our surface $S$ is of the form $z=g(x,y),$ it can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,g(x,y)⟩.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂x}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂g}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂g}{∂y}\\end{aligned}|=⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(x,y))\\cdot ({r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\frac{∂g}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂g}{∂y},\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401254 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ffab214-a531-5f16-9548-4aba64a14e09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∂z$ and $∂x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401256} {:answer/id #uuid "27be7768-bf01-5a25-8f76-a7b3aa6827e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∂x$ and $∂z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401257} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0b36ca-8d50-5d13-b2d4-01dff2d1189e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∂y$ and $∂z$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401258} {:answer/id #uuid "8c295efa-f53d-5757-9ea8-624ce01afe74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∂x$ and $∂y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401259} {:answer/id #uuid "401f8a2b-7596-5052-8ec8-449369280a45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∂y$ and $∂x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c295efa-f53d-5757-9ea8-624ce01afe74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$∂x$ and $∂y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401259} :answer-field/id #uuid "0585e533-2d5e-5fa5-b53e-85ce1c70e498" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident